{
  "slug": "neural-drift",
  "family": "tracks",
  "label": "Neural Drift",
  "note": "original — written in the idiom of Rameses B's melodic drum & bass, not transcribed from any track. B natural minor over the i-VI-III-VII vamp Bm G D A (breakdown Em Bm G A), 180 BPM (rowLen 3675, rows are 16ths so one pattern is two bars), 66 patterns / 132 bars, 176 s — 2:56, a full arrangement rather than a race loop. Form: 16-bar intro, 8-bar build, 32-bar drop, 16-bar breakdown, 8-bar build, 32-bar drop, 20-bar outro that thins back to pad and arp so the loop point is seamless. 7 ch: lead = the topline (two of them — A over the drops, B over the breakdown, held back for the drop's first 8 bars), arp = the cybernetic motion, 16ths in the drops and 8ths everywhere else; there is no hat channel, the arp does that job, pad = one held tone for each two bars, sub_bass = a clean sine root on each bar, reese = detuned syncopated mid bass, drops only, bass_drum_1 / snare_2 = the two-step break (kick on 1, snare on 3, kick on the & of 2 in the second bar) with ghost kicks under drop 2 and a 16th roll closing every section.",
